DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbiinnuuppttiimmee() and ggeettbbiinnuuppttiimmee() functions store the time elapsed since
     boot as a _s_t_r_u_c_t _b_i_n_t_i_m_e at the address specified by _b_t.  The
     mmiiccrroouuppttiimmee() and ggeettmmiiccrroouuppttiimmee() functions perform the same utility,
     but record the elapsed time as a _s_t_r_u_c_t _t_i_m_e_v_a_l instead.  Similarly the
     nnaannoouuppttiimmee() and ggeettnnaannoouuppttiimmee() functions store the elapsed time as a
     _s_t_r_u_c_t _t_i_m_e_s_p_e_c.  The ssbbiinnuuppttiimmee() and ggeettssbbiinnuuppttiimmee() functions return
     the time elapsed since boot as a _s_b_i_n_t_i_m_e___t.

     The bbiinnuuppttiimmee(), mmiiccrroouuppttiimmee(), nnaannoouuppttiimmee(), and ssbbiinnuuppttiimmee() functions
     always query the timecounter to return the current time as precisely as
     possible.  Whereas ggeettbbiinnuuppttiimmee(), ggeettmmiiccrroouuppttiimmee(), ggeettnnaannoouuppttiimmee(), and
     ggeettssbbiinnuuppttiimmee() functions are abstractions which return a less precise,
     but faster to obtain, time.

     The intent of the ggeettbbiinnuuppttiimmee(), ggeettmmiiccrroouuppttiimmee(), ggeettnnaannoouuppttiimmee(), and
     ggeettssbbiinnuuppttiimmee() functions is to enforce the user's preference for timer
     accuracy versus execution time.

